    "pipeline": "Step 1: DataRetrieverAgent -&gt; Retrieve the DEM for Richland County, South Carolina. -&gt; Step 2: DataRetrieverAgent -&gt; Retrieve the boundary for Richland County, South Carolina. -&gt; Step 3: RasterAgent -&gt; Use the Richland County boundary to clip the DEM, ensuring the output DEM is limited to the county's extent. -&gt; Step 4: VectorAnalysisAgent -&gt; Randomly generate 100 points within the Richland County boundary, ensuring the points are well-distributed across the entire county area. -&gt; Step 5: RasterAgent -&gt; Extract elevation values for each of the 100 randomly generated points using the clipped DEM, ensuring that each point's elevation is accurately recorded. -&gt; Step 6: MappingAgent -&gt; Generate a histogram of the elevation values from the 100 sampled points, ensuring the histogram includes appropriate axis labels and a title for clarity. -&gt; Step 7: MappingAgent -&gt; Overlay the 100 randomly generated points on the clipped DEM, ensuring the points are clearly visible and distinguishable on the map.",
